 ### [Adaptive Ray Marching with Temporal Reprojection](4840-adaptive-ray-marching-with-temporal-reprojection.md)
-Performs volume rendering by combining adaptive ray marching with temporal accumulation to reduce noise and flickering in animated scenes. It builds on [Adaptive Step Size Calculation](4671-adaptive-step-size-calculation.md) by using density thresholds to vary step size, and extends standard ray marching by reprojection of the previous frame's color and alpha into the current frame's screen space. It is distinct from sibling methods like [Ray Marching with Adaptive Step Count and Cone Sampling](4808-ray-marching-with-adaptive-step-count-and-cone-sampling.md) by relying on spatial reprojection rather than cone-based filtering for temporal stability [G]. Choose it when rendering animated volumetric scenes requiring temporal stability and noise reduction.
